  "query_preview": "..High pressure centered near Safford continues to \nprovide conflicting shear profiles and steering flow for our area. \nConvection today remains unorganized, but may come together for this \nevening, as outflow boundaries run into the deeper moisture south of \nthe Mogollon Rim. Nocturnal activity is a definite possibility for \neastern and southern Yavapai County this evening.\n\nHeading into Thursday and Friday, the high starts to move northward \ninto a more favorable position, but will then strengthen. This and \nthe possibility of debris cloud Thursday morning may keep convection \ndown a little bit, while temperatures stay hot. We are holding the \nEHW for the Colorado River elevations through Friday.\n\nBy the weekend and into early next week. The mid-level high remains \nin a favorable position, the cap weakens and moisture will continue \nto move north each day. We could very well be back into a high grade \nMonsoon pattern by early next week. Stay tuned.",
